WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.270
We have a Republican governor here in Massachusetts,
I've mentioned him before.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:11.970
His name is Charlie Baker, and he just signed
into law a bill giving every resident of Massachusetts

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.259
the option to vote by mail in the fall and
in the primaries leading up to the fall, if

00:00:17.259 --> 00:00:20.710
indeed that is what we want to do now.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:25.890
I have not hidden this from folks since the
start of the coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.939
I did not vote for Charlie Baker.

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:34.230
I'm not a Republican, but he has been a Republican
who has done a good job.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.500
Big picture on the Corona virus.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.230
And he's doing a lot of the right thing.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:44.670
So if I wanted to criticize, certainly he
could have started stay at home a little earlier.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:49.450
He could have talked about the importance
of wearing masks earlier.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:54.000
But Massachusetts is one of the few states
that has actually gotten the virus, what we

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.360
would call under control.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.880
As of right now, and this may change as cases
continue to explode in many states.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.460
My belief is that at some point, because you
can't block travel between states, or at least

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.340
it doesn't appear as though you can because
of the Constitution, we are going to have

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.340
a bleed over effect.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.520
I am fully expecting that as we get into late
summer and early fall, Massachusetts will

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.479
start to see more cases.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:24.590
But as of right now, we've seen dramatic declines
in cases and much of it has been under or

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:29.100
related to Republican Governor Charlie Baker's
leadership.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.180
And likewise, we now have a statewide vote
by mail, which is extremely important and

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.549
completely and obviously logical given the
corona virus pandemic.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:43.399
The secretary of state Web site now says,
quote, In July, meaning yesterday a new law

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:48.570
was passed to allow registered voters in Massachusetts
to vote by mail in any 20-20 election with

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.779
no excuse needed as required by the new law.

00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:56.109
A vote by mail application will be mailed
to every person who is registered to vote

00:01:56.109 --> 00:02:01.649
by July one and who had not already requested
an absentee ballot for the state primary or

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:03.469
for all elections this year.

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:07.969
A second mailing will be sent out in September
to all voters who have not already applied

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:10.759
for vote by mail for the November election.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.030
The applications are pre addressed to your
local election official and no postage is

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.030
necessary.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.550
So they're not just sending ballots around.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:24.160
The fear mongering from the Trumpy and right
is you just start sending ballots places.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.790
Anybody could fill them in and return them
and voter fraud and to let a little know all

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:28.950
that stuff.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:33.380
The reality is what they're doing is they're
taking the list of registered voters and sending

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:40.080
them applications for absentee ballots, which
you still must return.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.890
They must be delivered to the local election
office no later than four business days before

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.340
the election.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.650
This is the right move.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.020
This is simple.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.020
Just do it.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.050
Come on, states.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.050
Just do it.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.050
It's the right thing to do.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.390
It's the safe thing to do.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.820
And the problem is great.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.320
Massachusetts is doing it.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.260
Biden's going to win Massachusetts easily.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:07.750
In other words, what I mean is the states
that will be close where people may be scared

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.150
to vote in person because of the pandemic.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:17.240
Those are the states where you might actually
see a different outcome if there isn't vote

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.310
by mail.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.690
And many of those are the states that are
not interested in doing vote by mail.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.480
Now, fortunately, there are important states
that have done it.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:32.650
I believe Pennsylvania and Ohio, Arizona,
Texas has temporarily said fear of catching

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.260
the virus counts as a valid reason to vote
absentee mitt.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.220
Maybe Iowa, but this needs to be something
every state does.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.220
And and in fact, when we look at Trump careening
down hill in the polls and we look at everything

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.790
that's going on, his reelection depends on.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.790
Yes.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.160
Lying about the state of the economy, lying
about the state of the pandemic.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.470
But it also depends on suppressing the vote.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:00.780
And not allowing vote by mail is something
that could, in very material terms, dissuade

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.580
people from voting at all.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.660
Back to Charlie Baker in Massachusetts.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.240
Just just a little bit, because I anticipate
some of the emails I might receive.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.180
I have no delusions that Charlie Baker is
the height of progressivism.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.380
He's a former health insurance CEO.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.709
He's like a Mitt Romney type Republican, essentially.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:22.870
But it shouldn't be unusual that you have
a governor who listens to doctors in science.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.990
In other words, what's notable about the fact
that Charlie Baker, a Republican governor,

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:32.920
has mostly handled the virus correctly is
that it is unusual to have a Republican governor

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.700
who says, I'm going to do what the doctors
recommend.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.870
We have a pandemic.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.650
I'm going to make decisions based on science
and the medical community.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.139
I'm going to close things.

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:44.280
I'm going to allow vote by mail for everybody.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.180
The reason that this is newsworthy, the reason
that I'm talking in these terms of we have

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.940
a Republican governor who has actually managed
this pretty well, is that it's so rare when

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.810
you look at governors like Ron DeSantis in
Florida.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.470
I mean, just off the deep end, Greg.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.050
Abbott in Texas, and in particular, it actually.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:05.110
Abbott has come back to reality a little bit
saying we need masks.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.410
We should probably slow down or stop on bars.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.670
The lieutenant governor there, Dan Patrick,
has been particularly crazy.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:15.470
You've got Doug Deucy in Arizona and many,
many others.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:19.830
That is why it is so notable that a Republican
governor like Charlie Baker has done the right

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:20.830
thing.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.139
Now, I have some criticisms of what Charlie
Baker is doing.

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:25.990
I believe it is too early to do.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:30.510
Indoor dining phase three in Massachusetts
includes casinos and movie theaters.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.510
I just disagree.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.680
I'm not going to any of those.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.560
I've decided I'm comfortable with outdoor
dining right now.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.560
I'm not going inside.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.550
I mean, it's just it's not necessary.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:40.550
It's summer.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:48.370
There are articles that are linking card present
restaurant receipts, receipts to increased

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.370
case numbers.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.980
So it does seem like the indoor dining is
a problem.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:57.360
I think it's an unnecessary risk right now,
particularly when we don't listen.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.790
There may not even be a gap between wave one
and two, but we're anticipating more cases

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:02.790
in the fall.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.960
So I disagree with Baker on that.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.280
I think it's too early.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.240
Big picture managing it well.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.270
Vote by mail for everybody in Massachusetts.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.270
Absolutely.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.270
The right decision.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.290
I'm glad to see it.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.450
We now just need states where it'll be close
between Trump and Biden to adopt it as well.

